I couldn't apply the fix. A config-guard hook blocks agents from editing `.pi/extensions/**`, so I didn't try another route. Nothing was committed or pushed.

**The Codex finding (P2, `.pi/extensions/entire/index.ts:40`)**
Codex flagged one issue and I agree with it. Suppose `entire` is missing or exits before it reads its input. Writing a large payload to its stdin then fails with an `EPIPE` error. That error shows up later, outside the `try/catch`, and nothing listens for it, so it crashes Pi instead of the hook failing quietly. The fix is to attach an error handler to `child.stdin` before writing.

**The edit to make** (around line 40):
```ts
        );
        // EPIPE arrives asynchronously when `entire` is missing or exits before
        // reading stdin; without a listener it is thrown and kills Pi.
        child.stdin?.on("error", () => {});
        child.stdin?.end(JSON.stringify(data));
```
Ignoring the error is safe here: the `execFile` callback still runs and resolves with an empty string, so the hook stays optional.

**Caveat:** the file header says it is generated by `entire enable --agent pi` and is overwritten on the next install. Re-running that command will remove this fix, so the lasting fix belongs in Entire's Pi extension template. It may be worth reporting it there.

**Your uncommitted changes:** your working tree also has edits to `.claude/settings.json`, `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md`, plus a new `.entire/agent-guide.md`. These came from your Entire setup and I haven't touched them. When I commit, I'll include only the `.pi` file unless you tell me to add the others.

Once you've made the edit, tell me and I will:
1. commit only that file as `fix(pi): handle stdin EPIPE when forwarding Entire hooks`,
2. push it to `feat/entire-cli`,
3. reply on the review comment with the commit and resolve the thread.

